  "raw_text": "27\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb40\n):\n \nDebit sibrin âpu kira pana win: ...\n \n–\n \nDavid without having fear in turn said: ...\n \n/ David sin tener miedo\na su vez dijo: ...)\n\nSwira âpu\n \nkira\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nshamelessly, presumptuously\n \n/ sin vergüenza, presuntuosamente\n\nDiara âpu\n \n–\n \nnothing\n \n/\n \nnada\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n45:18\n):\n \ntasba na diara\n \nâ\npu kaia dukiara paskras kan\n \n–\n \ndid not create th\nis earth\n \nfor nothing\n \n/\n \nno creó esta\n\ntierra por nada\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nDiara âpu sa\n \n(a/t:\n \nDiara apia sa\n)\n \n–\n \nIt's nothing\n \n/ De nada\n \n(Alt:\n \nTrabil âpu\n \n–\n \nno trouble\n \n/ no hay problema\n)\n\nNit âpu\n \n–\n \nnot having the need\n \n/ no tener la necesidad\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb61\n):\n \nYang nani sans wala nit âpu sna\n \n–\n \nWe are not in need of another chance\n;\n \nWe don’t need another chance\n \n/ No\nnecesitamos otra oportunidad)\n\nNu âpu\n \n–\n \nnot known,\n \ndidn’t know\n,\n \nI don’t know\n \n/ desconocido, no sabía, no sé\n\n(Note/Nota: The conjugation varies depending on verb that follows\n \n/ La conjugación varía según el verbo que\n \nsigue\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nkm14/03\n):\n \nYawan baha nu âpu sa\n \n–\n \nWe aren’t knowing that; We don’t know that\n)\n\nUya nu âpu\n \n–\n \nnot well known, rare, uncommon\n\nPlun âpu\n \n–\n \nno food\n \n/\n \nsin comida\n\nTrabil âpu\n \n–\n \nno trouble, no problem\n \n/\n \nno hay problema\n\nUpla âpu\n \n–\n \nnobody\n \n/\n \nnadie\n\nAras\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhorse\n \n/\n \ncaballo\n\nAras\n \nâ\ni\nulra\n \n–\n \nrider of a horse\n \n/\n \njinete de un caballo\n\nAring\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhorn\n \n/\n \ncuerno\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmy46\n):\n \nSyîp aringka\n \n–\n \nsheep hor\nn\n \n/\n \ncuerno de oveja\n \n(referring to horns sounded at Jericho\n \n/\n \nrefiriéndose a los cuernos\n\nsonados en Jericó\n)\n\nArk\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nark\n \n/ arca\n\nLâ aisi daukan arkka\n \n(\nLâ nani auhbaia watla/watlika\n-\ndb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nArk of the Covenant\n \n/ Arca del Pacto\n\nArkbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto gnaw, to grind (teeth)\n \n/ roer, rechinar (dientes)\n\nArmagedan\n \n(\ndb,wqu\n;\n \nHar-Magedon\n-lrw\n;\n \nHarmagedon\n-dbta,dba,bh\n)\n \n–\n \nArmageddon\n \n/ Armagedón\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nNawas piua ra yang dîa dukia kau pain daukaia sip sna ki, Armagedan balbia kat bara Jehova pri ai sâkbia?\n \n–\n\nAt the present time, what am I able to do to serve better until Armageddon comes and Jehovah frees me?\n \n/ En la actualidad, ¿qué\npuedo hacer para servir mejor hasta que llegue el Armagedón y Jehová me libere?)\n\nArp\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nharp\n \n/ arpa\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb41\n):\n \nDebit arp pain kangbi kan\n \n–\n \nDavid played (\nliterally\n: was playing) the harp well\n \n/ David tocó (literalmente: estaba\ntocando) bien el arpa)\n\nAsa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \naxe\n \n/ hacha\n\nAsla\n \n–\n \nunited, close, all together, unanimous, in harmony\n \n/ unidos, todos juntos, unánimes, en armonia\n\nAsla aidrubaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto gather together, to meet together\n \n/ reunirse\n\nAsla aidrubanka\n \n–\n \nmeeting\n \n/ reunion\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n):\n \nUplika ra asla aidrubanka kum ra paiws.\n \n–\n \nInvite the person to a meeting.\n \n/ Invite a la persona a una\nreunion.)\n\nAsla Aidrubanka Watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nKingdom Hall\n \n/\n \nSalón del Reino\n\n(Note/Nota: A Kingdom Hall formerly was called\n \nKingka Lâka Watla\n \n/ Un Salón del Reino se llamaba anteriormente\n\nKingka Lâka Watla\n)\n\nAidrubanka Watla ra ulbi sakanka bâra ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe books at the Kingdom Hall, Kingdom Hall\nlibrary\n \n/ los libros en el Salón del Reino, biblioteca del Salón del Reino\n\nAsla Aidrubanka Watla Tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nAssembly Hall\n \n/\n \nSalón del Asambleas\n\nAsla daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto unite, to gather together, to get together, to put together as an organization, to unify\n \n/\nunirse, reunirse, juntarse como organización, unificar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-06/20-Lawana Nani 86:11\n):\n \nYang kupi asla dauks ninam kulkaia dukiara\n \n–\n \nUnify my heart in order to honor\nyour name\n \n/ Unifica mi corazón para honrar tu nombre)\n\nAsla dadaukra\n \n(\nkm04/2012\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nattendant\n \n/ acomodador\n\nAsla lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nunity\n \n/ unidad\n\n(Construct:\n \nAslika lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nbtq-9\n):\n \n¿Kangrigisan aslika lâka main kaikaia ba dîa muni sam taim karna kaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nWhy can it sometimes be\ndifficult to protect the unity of the congregation?\n \n/ ¿Por qué a veces puede ser difícil proteger la unidad de la\ncongregación?)",
